---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is HeadlessOS an operating system?",
    a: "No. The name is a nod to headless servers: machines with no screen that you manage through a terminal. HeadlessOS is an app that runs on your computer and gives those servers a desktop-style interface over SSH. Your server keeps its own operating system, and nothing on it is replaced.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does it install anything on my server?",
    a: "No. It connects over standard SSH and runs the same tools you would: ls, df, ps, docker, systemctl and so on. If a tool isn't there (say, Docker), the matching app tells you instead of installing it. No package, service or port is ever added; HeadlessOS only changes what you ask it to, and deleted files go to a trash folder you can restore from.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which servers does it work with?",
    a: "Any Linux machine you can reach over SSH: a cloud VPS, a home-lab box, a Raspberry Pi, a VM. Sign in with a key, your SSH agent, or a password.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need an AI or OpenAI key?",
    a: "No. Dashboards, files, Docker, processes, the terminal and admin tools all work without one; 31 built-in parsers handle everyday command output. Add a key in Settings to turn on the AI agent and to read output the parsers don't know. It works with OpenAI, Claude, or a local Ollama model that never leaves your machine.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it safe to point at a production server?",
    a: "It's built for that. The app only listens on localhost and asks for a per-install token. Saved passwords are encrypted on your disk. Commands go through an allowlist, the AI agent can only use a fixed set of checked actions, and file edits are backed up and verified before they're kept.",
  },
  {
    q: "How is it different from Cockpit, Webmin or Portainer?",
    a: "Those are installed on the server and served from it, so they need a package, a service and an open port on every machine. HeadlessOS runs on your computer instead, works across all your servers at once, and leaves each of them untouched.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it really free?",
    a: "Yes. HeadlessOS is MIT licensed and the whole thing is on GitHub. No account, no paid tier, no telemetry.",
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="section relative">
  <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.8fr)_minmax(0,1.2fr)] lg:gap-20">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <p class="rv eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="rv h2 mt-5 [--d:.05s]">Questions, answered.</h2>
      <p class="rv lede mt-6 [--d:.1s]">
        Something else? Ask in <a class="text-fg underline decoration-ink/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-ink" href="https://github.com/abhee235/headlessos/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rv divide-y divide-border border-y border-border [--d:.08s]">
      {
        faqs.map((f, i) => (
          <details class="faq group" open={i === 0}>
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left text-lg font-medium">
              {f.q}
              <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
            </summary>
            <p class="-mt-1 pb-6 pr-10 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .plus {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    transition: transform 0.25s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .plus::before,
  .plus::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 11px;
    height: 1.5px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--color-fg-muted);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }

  .plus::after {
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }

  .faq[open] .plus {
    background: rgb(var(--ink) / 0.06);
  }

  .faq[open] .plus::after {
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(0deg);
  }

  .faq summary:hover .plus {
    border-color: rgb(var(--ink) / 0.3);
  }
</style>
